{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/986539-the-masses-as-an-amplifier","id":986539,"title":"The Masses as an amplifier","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-10-12T20:23:01-07:00","id":986539,"title":"The Masses as an amplifier","content":"Half-baked idea here: you know how the Syndicate is able to use Personnel as an instrument? First mentioned in the Syndicate Revised Convention Book, but M20 has a box about it (though the name escapes me). What if the NWO can do something similar, utilizing a large number of properly conditioned Sleepers as a sort of \u201camplifier\u201d for their more subtle Procedures? What would be needed to do this sort thing, and what could it accomplish?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-12T20:57:15-07:00","id":986563,"title":"","content":"Sounds like the Cult Background on M20 p.310.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6384-frozenfishy","name":"Frozenfishy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6384_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"172"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-12T21:57:04-07:00","id":986578,"title":"","content":"Frozenfishy is correct, although using Personnel as an Instrument is also perfectly possible. So long as the underlings act according to the MiB's instructions, they are extensions of his or her Enlightened Will. But that's just for performing Inspired Science like normal. Cult is necessary for amplification.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-12T22:01:55-07:00","id":986580,"title":"","content":"Don't have the book open but I recall reading that some practices can use people as instruments.<br /> Not only the Cult background (that everyone can do) but also contacts, and retainers.<br /> <br /> The effect is not stronger but it is subtle to let your will work through the Unenlighted.<br /> <br /> Edit: M20 p. 595 Optional Rule Management and Human Resources \u201csidebar\u201c","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>So, this Zen Master walks up to a hot dog stand and says: &quot;Make me one with everything!&quot;","edited":{"userid":12022,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12022-nonsense","user":"Nonsense","date":".  Found it 10-13-2016, 01:20 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12022-nonsense","name":"Nonsense","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12022_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"815"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-12T22:12:55-07:00","id":986584,"title":"","content":"Maybe so; but I can't help thinking that the NWO ought to be especially good at something like this. Dominating the Masses is kinda their thing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-12T22:58:27-07:00","id":986596,"title":"","content":"Dominating the masses by propaganda<br /> VS<br /> Dominating the masses by dominating the masses?<br /> <br /> Method versus goal, I think.<br /> Of course the idea has potential. I think an extended working which changes public \u201cknowledge\u201c step by step is a great hook.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>So, this Zen Master walks up to a hot dog stand and says: &quot;Make me one with everything!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12022-nonsense","name":"Nonsense","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12022_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"815"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-13T13:10:33-07:00","id":986909,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/986539-the-masses-as-an-amplifier?p=986584#post986584\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Maybe so; but I can't help thinking that the NWO ought to be especially good at something like this. Dominating the Masses is kinda their thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>Indeed, they ought to be good at directing agents and personnel.<br /> <br /> An NWO could have Inspired Psychology as Mind and Inspired Sociology &amp; Statistics as Entropy. Directing groups of agents would involve treating them as manipulable and manageable system; any objectives to accomplish would be another system with which the first one would interact. Anyone bystanders that the agents interact with can be swept in into the manipulable system. Could be compared to management PC games. (<i>Europa Universalis</i>, <i>Syndicate</i>)<br /> <br /> Or psychology Mind, logic Entropy, philosophy Prime, statistics Time and sociology Correspondence.<br /> <br /> <u><i><b>Correspondence: Agents</b></i></u><br /> <b><i>Specialties: Information Gathering | Mindgames | Terror | Subtle Manipulations | Giving Aid</i></b><br /> <br /> Agent Correspondence allows directing agents from afar through various means - day-to-day instructions, constant advice given through a voice bead, directives issues for the long-term in advance, and of course envelopes with &quot;Open this in case of xxx, otherwise destroy it after y amount of time&quot;. At it's root lies the thesis that even with just one agent and one target (called 'subject' from now on), those involved are already a group \u2013 the NWO member, the agent he is working through, and the subject are all tied together; even if the subject is unaware of the NWO member.<br /> <br /> This Correspondence variant allows conjunctional Mind, Entropy, Time and Prime that are executed by the agent(s) with comparable results as if the NWO was personally present. (The fields for each Spheres could be: psychology Mind, logic Entropy, philosophy Prime, statistics Time.) As such, this is extremely useful for NWOs to be able to run several operations at once, while staying hidden.<br /> The number of agents is handled on a case to case basis. It can be as small as one or three, or as large as ten, twenty or even a hundred. In such large numbers the majority of the agents are many steps removed from both the NWO member and the Technocracy. Sometimes quality and depth of interaction is needed, while at other times setting the scene and operating over a long period of time through subtle details and interactions is the key.<br /> <br /> The number of <u>connection points</u> that need to be gathered is equal to the highest Sphere rank of the effect used. The rank of Agent Correspondence determines the max rank of an effect that can be used through it.<br /> If over twice the number of points is gathered, the effect gains -1 to difficulty.<br /> <br /> 1 point:<br /> Access to the subject's publications or written correspondence. Minimum: 40 A4 pages (font 12) on a topic that the subject feels strongly about or is regularly involved in.<br /> A minimum 4-5 hour video recording of the subject speaking, or a minimum 5-6 hour audio recording.<br /> An exhaustive list of the subject's friends and acquaintances.<br /> A timetable, and details about occupation(s) &amp; interests.<br /> Rundown on the most important details of the subject's past.<br /> <br /> 2 points:<br /> Psychological profile done.<br /> Constant and all-encompassing observation (tapped phones, shadowing, video monitoring, hacking personal computer).<br /> An agent is an acquaintance of the subject.<br /> <br /> 3 points:<br /> The NWO member using the Correspondence has interacted with for a minimum of one day - say, 8-12 hours of hanging out. Or 8-12 hours spread across several days and smaller interactions<i>.<br /> (This I especially like \u2013 it gives this scare factor of \u201cI trusted this guy for just one afternoon...then he stayed for the evening..and we talked politics \u2013 and soon it was Chantry politics. I didn't even think to ask him how he knows about Magick, because I was so tired...He was gone by the morning, and immediately I got that feeling that he saw right through me.\u201d)</i><br /> An agent has gained the subject's trust.<br /> An exhaustive record of the subject's life for at least a decade.<br /> <br /> 4 points:<br /> The NWO member using the Correspondence spent over 100 hours closely interacting with the subject.<br /> An agent is a close acquaintance \u2013 best friend, mentor, favored apprentice, lover, family member.<br /> An exhaustive record of the subject's life for at least 60 years.<br /> <br /> 5 points:<br /> The NWO member was \u2013 or still is! - a close acquaintance of the subject.<br /> The subject was interrogated and influenced in Room 101 for at least ten days.<br /> <br /> 6 points:<br /> The NWO member is having regular (at least 15 hours per week), personal contact with the subject.<br /> The subject was Processed.<br /> <br /> Multiple subjects can be targeted, but connection points must be shared by them at least in 75 %. So to target a group of three Mages with Entropy 5 effect you'd need four points worth of connection that are done for each of them in the same way - so let's say a psychological profile and constant &amp; all-encompassing observation. The remaining one connection point needed can be fulfilled in a different way for each of the subject Mages.<br /> <br /> <br /> The connection points do read like &quot;How much you are %^&amp;*ed cause the Technocracy has a bead on you.\u201d<br /> <br /> But do note and remember that Agent Correspondence can be used for the good of the target. In fact, it is used in good faith very often. Agents of the Technocracy - be they Enlightened, Extraordinary Citizens, or regular agents - almost always have a large number of connection points towards them. Extraordinary Citizens and Enlightened members of the Technocracy have almost all of the listed connection points. Unaware agents that aren't really part of the Technocracy still have information compiled about them, psychological profiles done, and NWO members often make sure to get to know them through the lenses of this Correspondence variant.<br /> Members and sympathizers of the Technocracy can be aided by this Sphere so that they better realize the Union's goals. They might benefit from aid in research and running businesses, advice &amp; support in field work, and specialized training.<br /> <br /> Tradition and Craft members have also received valuable support \u2013 such as Mind effects (sometimes boosted with Conjunctional Prime) that allowed them to see through manipulations and allowed to resist mind-influencing supernatural abilities. Information gathered about past events or predictions about what is to occur have also been provided on occasion. Through inscrutable means and borderline insulting manipulations an NWO member can even give Mages something akin to supernatural luck - which is, of course, simply manipulating the Mages to be at their most efficient selves.<br /> <br /> This Sphere is a major part why the Technocracy seems omnipresent to some Mages. The reality is that, wherever they are, they are constantly encountering agents carefully and artfully directed by the NWO.<br /> <br /> The variant can only be used for casting Conjunctional Effects of Mind, Entropy, Prime and Time Spheres. Remote viewing, enchanced perceptions or handling the issue of manipulating space are the province of Correspondence: Data.<br /> (Though the spectacular effect of multiple co-located selves can be readily replicated with right use of agents and psychological manipulations.)<br /> <br /> <br /> One of the most spectacular uses of this Sphere was when a young Mage's life was purposefully turned into a charade, with 90 % of his university class and the university staff being used by the Technocracy in varied and often brilliantly convoluted ways. (Such as extensively manipulating the students' board games club to sabotage any and all social relations he developed.) The idea was to accomplish several alternate, branching objectives, one of which was to discover the Apprentice's surely existing benefactors.<br /> <br /> The location and results of the experiment are highly classified. This is because the 'Apprentice' turned out to be a Widderslainte of the Tormented Essence. One thing surely learned is that one should not send unaware frat boys with a task of pushing around such a young man. And the most important lesson was that a skilled subject can turn around the presence of agents for their own benefit, even when he is outnumbered one to two hundred. (Especially when the subject has his back to the wall.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3254,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","user":"Muad'Dib","date":". 05-21-2018, 09:54 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-14T12:10:31-07:00","id":987365,"title":"","content":"There was an episode of Hustle where they managed to fool their mark into believing there was an up and coming company just by learning their route and strategically planting signs and conversations where they would notice them. There's also a scene in Night Watch (the Discworld Novel, I should specify) where a group strategically isolates all of their opponents at a party while making sure all the undecideds are moved into groups where they can be won over. What's interesting about both examples is that while they were enacted by people in the know, you could accomplish the same thing with completely unaware pawns.<br /> <br /> It actually seems like a good way of taking a complicated idea that requires direct mind control and converting it to a form of generalized mental influence.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}